# the client end-to-end tests

# LWJGL extracts the natives it needs out of the `-natives-linux` classifier jars on the classpath
# — there is no `-Djava.library.path` and no unpacked directory a launcher would have made — and it
# unpacks them beside the manifest, because the working directory of a `jals test` JVM is the
# project root. One directory per LWJGL version, written by every client boot.
.lwjgl/
